@startuml
title querychat: When Data Reaches the LLM

actor User
participant "Shiny UI" as UI
participant "Shiny Server" as Server
participant "querychat" as QC
participant "DuckDB" as DB
participant "LLM API" as LLM

== Scenario 1: User asks a question ==

User -> UI : "What is the survival rate?"
UI -> Server : on_user_submit()
Server -> QC : stream_response_async()
QC -> LLM : chat_history + user_message

LLM --> QC : **tool_call:**\nquerychat_query(\n  query = "SELECT AVG(survived)\n           AS rate FROM titanic"\n)

QC -> DB : execute SQL
DB --> QC : query result

QC --> LLM : **actual row data**\n[{"rate": 0.384}]

note over QC #EEFFEE
  querychat_query sends
  real data to the LLM API.
  This is how the LLM can
  interpret and explain results.
end note

LLM --> QC : "The survival rate is 38.4%."
QC --> Server : stream text
Server --> UI : chat message

== Scenario 2: extra_instructions trigger parallel calls ==

note over LLM #EEEEFF
  extra_instructions say:
  "use querychat_query to
  calculate row count and
  survival rate"
end note

User -> UI : "Show only first class"
UI -> Server : on_user_submit()
Server -> QC : stream_response_async()
QC -> LLM : chat_history + user_message

LLM --> QC : **two tool_calls in one turn:**

note over LLM, QC #FFFFDD
  1. querychat_update_dashboard(
       query = "SELECT * FROM titanic
                WHERE pclass = 1",
       title = "First class passengers")

  2. querychat_query(
       query = "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n,
                AVG(survived) AS rate
                FROM titanic WHERE pclass = 1")
end note

QC -> DB : execute update SQL
DB --> QC : ✅ valid
QC --> LLM : "Dashboard updated."

QC -> DB : execute query SQL
DB --> QC : result rows
QC --> LLM : [{"n": 216, "rate": 0.63}]

== Shiny reactive chain ==
QC -> Server : state.sql set → reactive invalidation
Server -> DB : qc_vals.df() re-runs SQL
DB --> Server : filtered DataFrame
Server --> UI : re-render table

LLM --> QC : "🎯 Filter: First class only\n📊 Stats: 216 rows | 63%\n💡 Insight: ..."
QC --> Server : stream text
Server --> UI : chat message with grounded stats

@enduml
